WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:08.508
The story I'm telling you is…

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:12.220
what I, Rohan Kishibe, heard
with my&nbsp;own ears.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.639
It was a horrifying incident.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:20.520
Do you know what a "confessional" is?

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.400
Every Italian church has one of those.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.528
It has two wooden boxes
that look like telephone booths.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.741
The parish priest gets
in the one with the curtains,

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.452
and the parishioner goes in the other&nbsp;box.

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.913
There's a little window
between the two&nbsp;boxes,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.916
and voices can go
through the window,&nbsp;but…

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:45.045
the priest and parishioner
cannot see each other.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:49.632
The window allows the parishioner
to confess their "sins"

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:54.220
with their privacy securely protected.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:01:00.560
You see, you can't keep a secret
hidden deep in your heart for years.

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:05.774
The graver the secret is,
the greater&nbsp;the suffering of the heart.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:11.071
A confessional is a place
to purge a soul&nbsp;of its sins.

00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:13.239
It was created
by the wisdom of people in the past.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:18.912
It's not allowed, but I took some photos
when the priest wasn't around

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.957
and looked closely at the design
and materials of the carvings.

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.711
And just for an experience,

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:30.381
I thought it wouldn't be a bad idea
if I could confess to a priest myself.

00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:31.966
So I went in the box.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.178
The actual experience
would bring reality into my work, you see.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.359
Huh?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:53.780
Father, I've come to make a confession.

00:01:54.656 --> 00:01:57.951
I have committed a great sin.

00:01:57.992 --> 00:01:58.952
Wha…

00:02:01.704 --> 00:02:05.500
I can't stand it anymore.
I've got to tell you, Father.

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.588
I can't sleep
without making a confession.

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:12.173
I swear it!

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:17.011
At that time, I didn't know the box
with the curtains was for the priest.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:20.682
This man mistook me for the priest.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.642
But…

00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:25.186
wasn't this a stroke of luck?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.815
What's his "great sin"?

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:32.360
I might as well
listen through to the&nbsp;end.

00:02:32.443 --> 00:02:35.155
A real experience
brings reality into my work.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.700
It doesn't matter
who listens to his confession.

00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:42.662
After all, it's the thought
that he confessed to the priest

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:45.081
that matters for this man.

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:48.001
Father, is there anything wrong?

